// §4.5.7 absdelay(input, td, maxdelay): "If td becomes greater than maxdelay,
// maxdelay will be used as a substitute for td", so maxdelay bounds every
// lookback the site can make. VerA sizes the site's history ring from it:
// ceil(maxdelay / 1ps) + 2 samples, at least 1024 and at most 16384
// (docs/IMPLEMENTATION.md, `codegen.hist_min_step`). This is the transmission
// line case: td = 1.5ns resolved at a 1ps step.
//
// HAND DERIVATION. The input is the ramp $abstime*1e12 (1 per ps), td =
// maxdelay = 1.5ns, on a uniform 1ps grid 0 .. 1600ps (1601 accepted points).
// Output(t) = Input(max(t - td, 0)) = max(t/1ps - 1500, 0): 0 through 1500ps,
// then 1 .. 100. Every query lands on a grid point, so linear interpolation is
// exact. At t = 1600ps the query t - td = 100ps is 1500 accepted samples old.
//
// THE LEGAL NEIGHBOUR is the refusal: the same delay WITHOUT maxdelay keeps
// the 1024-sample ring and ends the run with E1012 at the 1025th point
// (absdelay_history_underrun_is_fatal.va pins that exit on a 1ns grid). A ring
// that did not grow would do that here too, before t = 1600ps.
//
//! lrm 4.5.7
//! bias V(n) = 0
//! checks 1601
//! time 0p, 1p, 2p, 3p, 4p, 5p, 6p, 7p, 8p, 9p, 10p, 11p, 12p, 13p, 14p, 15p, 16p, 17p, 18p, 19p, 20p, 21p, 22p, 23p, 24p, 25p, 26p, 27p, 28p, 29p, 30p, 31p, 32p, 33p, 34p, 35p, 36p, 37p, 38p, 39p, 40p, 41p, 42p, 43p, 44p, 45p, 46p, 47p, 48p, 49p, 50p, 51p, 52p, 53p, 54p, 55p, 56p, 57p, 58p, 59p, 60p, 61p, 62p, 63p, 64p, 65p, 66p, 67p, 68p, 69p, 70p, 71p, 72p, 73p, 74p, 75p, 76p, 77p, 78p, 79p, 80p, 81p, 82p, 83p, 84p, 85p, 86p, 87p, 88p, 89p, 90p, 91p, 92p, 93p, 94p, 95p, 96p, 97p, 98p, 99p, 100p, 101p, 102p, 103p, 104p, 105p, 106p, 107p, 108p, 109p, 110p, 111p, 112p, 113p, 114p, 115p, 116p, 117p, 118p, 119p, 120p, 121p, 122p, 123p, 124p, 125p, 126p, 127p, 128p, 129p, 130p, 131p, 132p, 133p, 134p, 135p, 136p, 137p, 138p, 139p, 140p, 141p, 142p, 143p, 144p, 145p, 146p, 147p, 148p, 149p, 150p, 151p, 152p, 153p, 154p, 155p, 156p, 157p, 158p, 159p, 160p, 161p, 162p, 163p, 164p, 165p, 166p, 167p, 168p, 169p, 170p, 171p, 172p, 173p, 174p, 175p, 176p, 177p, 178p, 179p, 180p, 181p, 182p, 183p, 184p, 185p, 186p, 187p, 188p, 189p, 190p, 191p, 192p, 193p, 194p, 195p, 196p, 197p, 198p, 199p, 200p, 201p, 202p, 203p, 204p, 205p, 206p, 207p, 208p, 209p, 210p, 211p, 212p, 213p, 214p, 215p, 216p, 217p, 218p, 219p, 220p, 221p, 222p, 223p, 224p, 225p, 226p, 227p, 228p, 229p, 230p, 231p, 232p, 233p, 234p, 235p, 236p, 237p, 238p, 239p, 240p, 241p, 242p, 243p, 244p, 245p, 246p, 247p, 248p, 249p, 250p, 251p, 252p, 253p, 254p, 255p, 256p, 257p, 258p, 259p, 260p, 261p, 262p, 263p, 264p, 265p, 266p, 267p, 268p, 269p, 270p, 271p, 272p, 273p, 274p, 275p, 276p, 277p, 278p, 279p, 280p, 281p, 282p, 283p, 284p, 285p, 286p, 287p, 288p, 289p, 290p, 291p, 292p, 293p, 294p, 295p, 296p, 297p, 298p, 299p, 300p, 301p, 302p, 303p, 304p, 305p, 306p, 307p, 308p, 309p, 310p, 311p, 312p, 313p, 314p, 315p, 316p, 317p, 318p, 319p, 320p, 321p, 322p, 323p, 324p, 325p, 326p, 327p, 328p, 329p, 330p, 331p, 332p, 333p, 334p, 335p, 336p, 337p, 338p, 339p, 340p, 341p, 342p, 343p, 344p, 345p, 346p, 347p, 348p, 349p, 3